          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A notion of
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-module
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-vector space) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"}> vector space
            ).
          %p
            There are various different notions of
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            One notion is: an
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
            this is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baez-Crans+2-vector+space"} Baez-Crans 2-vector space
          %p
            Another is, recursively: an
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-bimodules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            this is envisioned in (
            %a{:href => "#FHLT"}> FHLT, section 7
            ), details are in spring. It includes the previous concept as a special case.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
            this subsumes various other definitions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-vector+space"} 2-vector space
            that are in the literature, such as notably the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kapranov-Voevodsky+2-vector+space"} Kapranov-Voevodsky 2-vector space
          %p
            We sketch the iterative definition of
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Assume that a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-category
            is chosen for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            (for instance
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-category"} (n,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            objects and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
            object in a symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} algebra in an (∞,1)-category
          %p Then we have the following recursive (rough) definition:
          %p
            fix a ground
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a 0-vector space over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is an elemment of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-category"} 0-category
                of 0-vector spaces is the set
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      0 Vect_k = k
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 Vect_k
                is just
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            %li
              %p
                For
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mi Vect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n Vect
                of
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  \-vector spaces
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Vect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)Vect
                and morphisms bimodule objects in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Vect
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)Vect
          %p
            Here we think of an algebra object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in (n-1)Vect
            as a basis for the
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
          %p
            With this definition we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 Vect
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
          %p
            More generally, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            here be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,0)Vect_k := k
                – a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Vect_k := k Mod
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
                of modules over that ring spectrum;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)Vect_k := (\infty,n-1) Mod
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,n)-category
                of modules over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Mod
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n-1)Mod
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Following the
            %a{:href => "IteratedModules"} above idea
            we have the following definition.
          #nVectViaALgObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Fix a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              (usually taken to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              if one speaks of “vector spaces” instead of just
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ∞-ring
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,n)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n Vect_k
              of
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                \-vector spaces
              as follows (the bi-counting follows the pattern of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-categories"} (n,r)-categories
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,0)
                \-vector space
              is an element of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is an ordinary ring, then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-category"} 0-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 Vect
              is the underlying set of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              using the product structure on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is more generally an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ∞-ring
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C0%29-category"} (∞,0)-category
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              = succeed "-vector" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,0)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              itself:
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,0)Vect_k \simeq k
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-vector+space"} (∞,1)-vector space
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} ∞-module
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "-vector" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mi Mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\infty,1)Vect_k := k Mod
                    \\,,
            %p
              the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a field ordinary
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              are a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(∞,1)-category
              of this:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1Vect_k \hookrightarrow (\infty,1)Vect_k
              \.
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                \-vector space
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} algebra object in the symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Vect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n-1)Vect
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule+object"} bimodule object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} Higher morphisms
              are defined recursively.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            replaced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            this appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Schreiber"}> Schreiber, appendix A
            ) and then with allusion to more sophisticated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categorical
            tools in (
            %a{:href => "#FHLT"}> FHLT, def. 7.1
            ).
          %p
            Notice that FHLT say “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            \-algebra” instead of “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-vector space”, but only for the reason (p. 29) that
          %blockquote
            %p
              The discrepancy between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              (the algebra level) and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              [the algebra level] – for which we apologize – is caused by the fact that the term “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-vector space” has been used for a much more restrictive notion than our
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#vector_spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-vector spaces
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-vector+space"} (∞,1)-vector space
            for more.
          %h3#2modules 2-Modules
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The symmetric monoidal 3-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_k^b = 2 Mod_k
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-modules"} 2-modules
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
                  over
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodules"} bimodules
                  of associative algebras;
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  of bimodules;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                  are bimodule homomorphisms.
            %p
              We think of this equivalently as its essential image in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect_k Mod
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is a placeholder for its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+category"} module category
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Mod
                            %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_A
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  is a placeholder for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi A
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi A
                            %mi N
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Mod_A \stackrel{(-) \otimes_A N }{\to} Mod_B
              %li
                %p
                  a bimodule homomorphism is a placeholder for a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  of two such functors.
            %p
              If we think of an algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in terms of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Vect
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mod_A \simeq Vect Cat(B A, Vect)
                    \\,.
            %p Comparing this for the formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V \simeq Set(S,k)
            %p
              for a
              = succeed "-vector" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  think of the algebra objects appearing in the above as being
                  %em bases
                  for a higher vector space;
              %li
                %p
                  think of the bimodules as being higher
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrices
          %h3#3modules 3-Modules
          %p
            A
            %em 3-vector space
            according to def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#nVectViaALgObjects"}
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                equipped with an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\otimes A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
                defining the 2-multiplication, and a left
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                defining the unit.
          %p
            Equivalently this is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquiunital+sesquialgebra"} sesquiunital sesquialgebra
          %p Classes of examples come from the following construction:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %em commutative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                becomes a 3-vector space.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
                canonically becomes a 3-vector space (amplified in
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#FHLT"} FHLT, p. 27
              %p
                More generally: every
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hopfish+algebra"} hopfish algebra
          %h3#4modules 4-Modules
          %p
            Next, an algebra object internal to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
